# Korenix JetI/O 6550.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Korenix JetI/O 6550 Industrial Intelligent Ethernet I/O Server
# | 
# | Source: JetI/O 6550 User's Manual V1.6
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (Ethernet port 502)
# | FC03: Read/Write Holding Registers — configuration, control, rule engine, P2P (below)
# | FC04: Read Input Registers — DI counter values ch0-13 (addr 0x0000-0x001D, u32 hi/lo pairs)
# | FC02: Read Discrete Inputs — DI status ch0-13 (addr 0x0000-0x000D, 1-bit per channel)
# | FC01/FC05: Read/Write Coils — DO ch0-7 (addr 0x0000-0x0007, 1-bit per channel)
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Active I/O data is in FC04 (DI counters), FC02 (DI states), FC01 (DO).
# | FC03 holding registers are configuration only.
# | 
# | Rule engine (16 rules, 0-15): each rule has IF condition (up to 4 DI, AND/OR)
# | THEN action (up to 4 DO). Condition operators: 0=ON,1=OFF,2=Lo→Hi,3=Hi→Lo,
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Korenix
@model=JetI/O 6550
@description=14-DI + 8-DO digital I/O Ethernet server, Modbus/TCP. FC03 holding regs: watchdog (0-2), firmware/name/reset (3-5), DO coil power-on/safe (6-7), DI counter control (8-14), DO pulse control (15-50), rule engine rules 0-7 (51-130), P2P/SNMP config (89-130 overlap), extended Flash rules 8-15 + P2P IPs (500-578), error codes (595-604). FC04: DI counter values ch0-13 addr 0-29 (u32 hi/lo). FC02: DI status ch0-13 addr 0-13 (1-bit). FC01: DO ch0-7 addr 0-7 R/W (1-bit). 16-rule IF-THEN logic engine; P2P peer-to-peer I/O mirroring.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/korenix-jetio-6550.toml; Source: JetI/O 6550 User's Manual V1.6. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

